  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1141 AM CST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nThe upper ridging mentioned in the short term discussion will push \neast across our forecast area through Friday. Subsidence below the \nridging will keep conditions dry, however there will be no impact on \ntemperatures with highs in the 60s to lower 70s both Thursday and \nFriday. Chances for precipitation return this weekend with an upper \npattern change. Models indicate an upper trough will swing across \nthe Desert Southwest/northern Mexico shifting flow aloft to the \nsouthwest through Saturday. The trough will quickly pass overhead \nSunday and deamplify as it exits to the east as a negatively tilted \ntrough swings across the Rockies. As this secondary trough tracks \nacross the Central Plains, upper ridging will build over the Desert \nSouthwest and flow aloft will shift to the northwest effectively \ncutting off subtropical moisture. Ridging will keep conditions next \nweek dry, however temperatures look to cool with highs possible in \nthe 50s by Monday.",
